ontal and vertical flows. On the circle, pair equal-length small arcs related by a quarter turn. Their horizontal and vertical normal projections have matching geometric weights. The compressing contribution is three times as large as the opposing contribution. There is net inflow, so the flux of $\\mathbf V$ is negative.\n\nThe normal component of a sum is the sum of its normal components. Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi_C(\\mathbf F)&=\\Phi_C(\\mathbf U)+\\Phi_C(\\mathbf V)\\\\\n&=0+\\Phi_C(\\mathbf V).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![Field vectors and outward normals](images/30/302e60144c8acf46ec5c68465fd56fbf67a0f006c1e407ee319c16b028d9c6c9.png)\n\nReversing traversal changes neither the outward normal nor arc length. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\Phi_{-C}=\\Phi_C<0.\n$$\n\nEvaluate each statement:\n\n- The flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $-C$ is not negative. **false**.\n- The flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $C$ is negative. **true**.\n- The flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $C$ is nonzero. **true**.\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "989049e9-1fc0-5b58-a112-a35410ea473c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718172} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd550cb-84ca-5ce3-9ea8-edb0194865aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718174}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718174} :answer-field/id #uuid "63336547-1219-5090-b21c-0530850b7bf7" :answer-field/key "The flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $C$ is nonzero." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4873a746-a481-500f-88c7-3665ee27d4d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718163} {:answer/id #uuid "c241abf6-1fd9-5fee-8348-eb81e3d2b6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718183}